             text="They sound alike but they're different. Authentication asks who you are. Authorization asks what you're allowed to do. Checking only the first is a classic security bug: any logged-in user could edit anyone's data.\n\nCheck permission on the server, for every request. Never rely on the interface hiding a button. And don't invent your own password storage or tokens; real projects use tested libraries.",
